            <ArticleTitle>Endovascular repair of growing chronic type B aortic dissection with a vascular plug.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>648-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1258/ar.2012.110605</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the successful endovascular repair of a growing chronic type B aortic dissection using an Amplatzer Vascular Plug II. A 44-year-old man, with previous medical history of aortic surgery and stenting complained of vague back pain. An approximately 5-mm entry remained in the stented segment of the aorta on computed tomography (CT). Endovascular closure of the entry with a Vascular Plug was uneventful. A 3-month follow-up CT showed no leak, complete false lumen thrombosis in the thoracic segment, shrinkage of the false lumen, and a reduced diameter of thoracic aorta.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
